d011-8836-5efd-ab3b-ba09c700a3e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188542 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186185532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188542 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119161" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188542 #edb/ref 1071 "The area of a circle increases at a rate that's proportional to the square of its radius. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the radius, $r(t)$, in this process. Assume that $K > 0$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188542 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c8d1bea5-b961-5d22-9bfd-ba62f26db131" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188912 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186187548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188912 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188912 #edb/ref 1071 "Tom's spherical basketball has a hole in it. Its volume decreases at a rate that's proportional to its surface area. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the radius, $r(t)$, of the ball. Assume that $k > 0$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188912 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "216b8c3f-43b1-55fb-bffc-27ac09c14aab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188913 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186187554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188913 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188913 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38324" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188913 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188913 #edb/ref 1071 "The size of a bush growing in a schoolyard is being monitored. The area $A\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}$ of the bush at any given moment grows at a rate that's directly proportional to the area at that moment. Additionally, $2\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}$ of the bush is cut away every month.\nWhat is the differential equation that describes the rate of change in the area of the schoolyard bush at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time in months since it started growing?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188913 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2aeb7023-942d-59e4-9752-79902203013d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188913 #edb/ref 1074 "The rate of change in the area of the bush per month increases in proportion to $A$ and decreases by $2.$ The differential equation that describes this is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA-2,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is the (positive) constant of proportionality." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186187926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188975 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80491" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188975 #edb/ref 1071 "The volume of a cube decreases at a rate that's proportional to its surface area. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the side length, $s(t)$, in this process. Assume that $K > 0$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188975 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "87dafc6b-b002-5f20-a4d1-b738e1cc353e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189054 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189054 #edb/ref 1061 1853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189054 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "da66f4c9-69eb-512a-b43d-9289b5f8fb5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189054 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189104 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189104 #edb/ref 1061 38001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189104 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "37206e3d-9800-567e-82f6-eed74a977f1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189104 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189105 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189105 #edb/ref 1061 38002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189105 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9da430dc-8eca-5286-8278-c764eba32b5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189105 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189107 #edb/ref 1061 38012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189107 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "53525e67-0e77-588f-88a9-1bda7f5964de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189107 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188291 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189108 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189108 #edb/ref 1061 38016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189108 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ccce909c-08ed-53ce-a30b-e357e8de3d59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189108 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189245 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189245 #edb/ref 1061 53348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189245 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d499c1d3-7173-5509-b128-c42561cce342" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189245 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189375 #edb/ref 1064 "When constructing a differential equation to model a particular phenomenon, we sometimes combine several pieces of information to create the correct model.\n\nConsider the following situation:\n\n*The common cold virus spreads through a particular country. The rate at which the number of infected people increases is **proportional** to the **square of the time** $t$ (in days) since the outbreak started. Additionally, $100$ infected people **recover from the virus each day**.*\n\nWe want to find a differential equation that models $P(t),$ the number of infected people. We note the following:\n\n- The statement describes the *rate* at which the *number of infected people* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity $$\\dfrac{\\textrm d P}{\\textrm d t}.$$\n- The rate at which the number of infected people increases is **proportional** to the **square of the time** $t.$ Therefore, if $I(t)$ represents the rate at which infections increase, then $$I(t) = kt^2,$$ where $k$ is a positive constant.\n- Additionally, $100$ infected people **recover from the virus each day**. Therefore, if $D(t)$ represents the rate at which infections decrease, then $$D(t) = 100.$$\n\nTherefore, the differential equation that describes this phenomenon is as follows: $$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t} & ={{k{t}^{2}-100}_{⏟}}_{I(t)-D(t)}\\end{aligned}$$\n\nAlthough we introduced the functions $I(t)$ and $D(t)$ here, we can usually write down the appropriate differential equation straight away. Let's see an example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189375 #edb/ref 1065 6270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189375 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8a7ad3b5-e4de-56c0-8fc9-8a9b2c976094" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189375 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189439 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's recall some basic facts from geometry in the $xy$-plane:\n\n- The distance between the point $(x,y)$ and the origin $(0,0)$ equals $\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}.$\n- The (smallest) distance between the point $(x,y)$ and the $x$-axis equals $|y|.$\n- Similarly, the (smallest) distance between the point $(x,y)$ and the $y$-axis equals $|x|.$\n- The slope of the line that passes through $(x,y)$ and the origin equals $\\dfrac{y}{x}.$\n\nWe sometimes need to use these basic facts when constructing differential equations described in a geometric context.\n\nLet's see an example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189439 #edb/ref 1065 8152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189439 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b03d6daa-af90-5f14-bf0f-929da8526673" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189439 #edb/ref 1067 "Recalling Some Facts From Elementary Geometry" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373715 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373715 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119189" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373715 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373715 #edb/ref 1071 "A scientist experiments with bacteria. The number of bacteria $B(t)$ in his experiment increases at a rate proportional to the number of bacteria at that moment. Additionally, due to environmental conditions, $250$ bacteria die every hour.\nWhat is the differential equation that describes the rate of change in the population of bacteria at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time in hours?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373715 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "30342124-81c8-53c0-b466-7bdc97912fd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373715 #edb/ref 1074 "The rate of change in the number of bacteria per hour increases in proportion to $B$ and decreases by $250.$ The differential equation that describes this is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=kB-250,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a (positive) constant of proportionality." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373716 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373716 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373716 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186373721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373716 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "497d4119-43d8-54a4-9409-872704d2bb05" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373717 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-kB-250,\\,k>0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373717 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373717 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4e7871ed-5cf7-50d7-886e-dbe5d153b9b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373718 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=kB-250t,\\,k>0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373718 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373718 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e7dfbae4-5b1d-5477-8e3d-b60d9435539f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373719 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=kB+250,\\,k>0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373719 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373719 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "44700f85-a5f3-5ba3-b3be-7e5afb18cd1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373720 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k{B}^{2}-250,\\,k>0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373720 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373720 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3a6edff6-d4af-5c48-a54d-c54c74640bbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373721 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=kB-250,\\,k>0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373721 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373721 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "724c6b53-f1f0-58e4-8ecf-980b9958ff52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373799 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373799 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143125" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373799 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373799 #edb/ref 1071 "The volume of a cube increases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the length of its edge. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the edge length, $s(t),$ in this process. Assume that $K>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373799 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "deb34ff2-c563-5932-95e2-cff733776593" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373799 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **volume** of a cube **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **length of its edge**.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume $V$ of a cube* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ *increases* at a rate that's *inversely proportional to the length of its edge.* Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe volume $V$ of a cube is given by\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({s}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =3{s}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{s} \\\\ 3{s}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{s} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{3{s}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK=\\frac{k}{3}>0\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{K}{{s}^{3}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373800 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373800 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373800 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186373803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373800 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "20ed6ed5-0a52-5e29-8c5e-f028a3e0baf7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373801 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=K{s}^{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373801 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373801 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "49a327b9-75a5-53f6-8b43-cf618bcf3524" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373802 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{K}{s}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373802 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373802 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1df99bf7-929a-5903-abcf-591bb526f29e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373803 #edb/ref 1