frac{k}{r}\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe area of a circle is given by \n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =2\\pi r\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k}{r} \\\\ 2\\pi r\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k}{r} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k}{2\\pi {r}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK=\\frac{k}{2\\pi }>0\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{K}{{r}^{2}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373821 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373821 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373821 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373821 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373821 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373821 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373821 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373821 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186373823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373821 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "96d00b91-6897-5427-9c98-70d18a8a25c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373822 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-Kr" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373822 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373822 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "44aa8350-415a-5f9c-b0de-81bc08e238c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373823 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{K}{{r}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373823 #edb/