ac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}$ *decreases* at a rate *proportional to the area of the square*. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=-kA\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe side length of a square is given by \n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt{A}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{A}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{A}}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} & =-kA \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{A}}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-kA \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-2k{A}^{3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK=2k>0\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-K{A}^{3/2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373842 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373842 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373842 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186373845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373842 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "da7d7a9b-3a3b-5028-ad76-6fd5d5b5cf8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373843 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-K{A}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373843 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373843 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a0fb4ff0-8aba-56c6-bf18-44b6befa2526" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373844 #edb/